Goal: add a --tsv flag to the CLI so tab-separated stdin is parsed with a tab separator, while runs without the flag behave exactly as they do now.

Context (current repo state):
- bin/csv2json.js reads all of stdin (readFileSync(0, 'utf8')) and writes `${JSON.stringify(parse(text))}\n`. It ignores process.argv.
- src/parse.js exports parse(text, sep = ','), which already splits each line on sep and rows on /\r?\n/.
- test/csv.test.js uses node:test and has a 'cli' test that runs execFileSync('node', ['bin/csv2json.js'], { input, encoding: 'utf8' }) from the repo root.
- package.json has "test": "node --test".
- README.md shows only `node bin/csv2json.js < table.csv`.

Steps:
1. In bin/csv2json.js, check whether '--tsv' appears anywhere in process.argv.slice(2). If it does, call parse(text, '\t'); otherwise call parse(text) exactly as today. Keep the output line unchanged (JSON.stringify of the result, then a single newline). Do not change handling of other or unknown arguments, do not add --help, --sep or --delimiter, and do not add auto-detection or quoting rules.
2. Leave src/parse.js as it is unless you find a real need; the existing sep parameter is enough.
3. In test/ (for example test/csv.test.js), add node:test tests that run bin/csv2json.js with the --tsv argument on tab-separated input and assert the exact stdout. Cover at least:
   - input 'a\tb\n1\t2\n' with --tsv -> '[{"a":"1","b":"2"}]\n'
   - input 'name\tnote\nx\thello, world\n' with --tsv -> '[{"name":"x","note":"hello, world"}]\n'
   - input 'a\tb\n1\t2\n3\t4\n' with --tsv -> '[{"a":"1","b":"2"},{"a":"3","b":"4"}]\n'
   - input 'a\tb\n1\t2\n' without the flag -> the JSON of [{"a\tb":"1\t2"}] plus '\n' (i.e. '[{"a\\tb":"1\\t2"}]\n' as a JS string literal)
   Keep the existing parse and cli tests passing.
4. Update README.md: keep the CSV example and add a --tsv section with an example invocation such as `node bin/csv2json.js --tsv < table.tsv`, stating that --tsv reads tab-separated input (fields split on a single tab character).
5. Verify from the repo root before opening the PR:
   - printf 'a\tb\n1\t2\n' | node bin/csv2json.js --tsv; echo "exit=$?"  -> [{"a":"1","b":"2"}] then exit=0
   - printf 'name\tnote\nx\thello, world\n' | node bin/csv2json.js --tsv  -> [{"name":"x","note":"hello, world"}]
   - printf 'a\tb\n1\t2\n3\t4\n' | node bin/csv2json.js --tsv  -> [{"a":"1","b":"2"},{"a":"3","b":"4"}]
   - printf 'a,b\n1,2\n' | node bin/csv2json.js  -> [{"a":"1","b":"2"}]
   - printf 'a\tb\n1\t2\n' | node bin/csv2json.js  -> [{"a\tb":"1\t2"}] (with \t as the literal JSON escape)
   - npm test  -> exits 0
6. Open one pull request containing the CLI change, the new tests and the README update.